33,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The late-turn pool is empty. Overtime is covering everything. We cannot extend hours.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, the data shows mid-city runs are slower, but platforms clear fast.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the capital ledger is ring-fenced. We have no new money for operations.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, the late-evening pilot eight years ago actually made money.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the ferry and rail data terms are still broken. Integration is a myth.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, that pilot was small. We have no spare crews for a full extension.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, if connections are the bottleneck, fixing the mid-city corridor helps everyone.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, if the data isn't shared, a fare platform is just expensive software.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the accessibility works finished on time. The bus lanes failed.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the pre-war shells are a trap. Bidders are pricing in weeks of delay.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, the bus corridor needs roadway crews. They are a third below establishment.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, but the journey audits say waiting is the problem, not the bus speed.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the ticketing fees are eating the paving budget. We can't afford both.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the lift maintenance contract has spare capacity. That is a good sign.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, but the station access upgrades hit the pre-war shells. That is where the delays are.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,We have no crews for night service or bus lanes. Station access is the only viable option.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I agree. The mid-city bus is a trap. Station access fixes the connection wait.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the capital ledger is tight, but the lift contract has slack. It is the safest bet.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, the history supports it. The accessibility works succeeded. The bus lanes did not.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, I am wary of the shells, but the data terms for fares are broken. Access is best.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
